  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Cynergy Professional Systems reported $252M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Cynergy Professional Systems received 269 awards this fiscal year so far, with an average award size of $936K. Cynergy Professional Systems obligations are up 248.2% year over year. Cynergy Professional Systems has seen funding concentrate in recent years: FY21 obligations were $67M, FY22 obligations were $90.8M, FY23 obligations were $85.9M, FY24 obligations were $95M, and FY25 obligations were $72.3M. Cynergy Professional Systems has most of its FY2026 obligations coming from the Department of Homeland Security, the Department of Justice, and the Department of Veterans Affairs. Cynergy Professional Systems sells primarily in the Other Computer Related Services market, followed by Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing and Computer Systems Design Services. Cynergy Professional Systems presents a mix of large and small awards this year, and the current-year totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date reporting.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did Cynergy Professional Systems obligations jump in FY2026?",
        "body": "Cynergy Professional Systems obligations rose to $252M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $102M and the Department of Justice obligated $76.7M, which together account for a large share of the increase. The Other Computer Related Services market supplied $236M of FY2026 obligations, indicating concentration in that NAICS. FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and not full-year results."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Cynergy Professional Systems top buyers and markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security, the Department of Justice, and the Department of Veterans Affairs are the top three buyers in FY2026 to date. Other buying agencies include the Department of Defense, the General Services Administration, and the Department of State. The largest market is Other Computer Related Services at $236M, followed by Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $5.6M and Computer Systems Design Services at $2.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
